    "body": "## Problem and changes\n\nThis implements three frozen tasks from #78 against draft integration #56:\n\n- **05:** The protocol CI command stopped at argument parsing because no current-source manifest was supplied. Prepare a fresh archive-v4 manifest from actual source and reviewed build inputs, revalidate its bytes and SHA-256 with the original validator, then pass the explicit policy/manifest/hash into the original runner.\n- **06:** Administrator invitation completions could survive dialog, session or input changes. Bind result and busy ownership to the current session, dialog, request and draft; discard obsolete responses without replaying an issued POST.\n- **07:** Suppression-removal JSON accepted unbounded/incomplete input. Apply a 64 KiB body limit and the original strict single-document decoder while preserving authorization, audit-reason byte limits and transactional deletion.\n\n## Validation and review\n\nIntegrated product `1cc2d50c883a016e5528c365452012ea149245f1`; final local delivery `d9d19038e255871f836273daad56b7a80fac5743`, exact tree `2ecb9c22bfca6f6593f156dc6788bde6d72cc061`.\n\n- HTTP selection: **32 leaf PASS**, race enabled, 0 FAIL/SKIP.\n- Protocol preparation, original protocol and backend-continuation controls: **70 methods PASS**, 0 FAIL/SKIP.\n- Invitation, deletion and permission UI: **49 PASS**, 0 FAIL/SKIP. Full tsc then found one unsupported test-query option; removing that unrecognized option preserved exact name matching. Corrected invitation file: **22 PASS**, and full nonincremental tsc exits 0. These are separate runs.\n- Actual preparation and original archive-v4 validation succeed. With no local PG DSN, the subsequent original runner correctly exits 1; no real PG pass is claimed.\n- Independent native-subagent review accepts 05 and 06 including the type correction; root accepts 07.\n\nOriginal timeouts, source/archive rejection, non-idempotent request transport, permission rules and PostgreSQL transaction boundaries remain intact. Raw scoped evidence and source pins are in `docs/company-mail/evidence/R5-NEXT-20261008/round2`.\n\nAfter this integration: **7/10 new bounded tasks complete, 3 remaining; original parents remain 10/171 accepted, 161 remaining**. Final catalogs follow all ten product tasks; full CI, PG/opt-in fixtures, private frontend fixture, dependency audit and M/G0 remain open. This PR targets the existing draft integration and does not promote it to main.",
    "title": "fix: complete three R5 protocol and administrator reliability tasks",
